  "description": "The failure ladder of 2500-WRITE-REJECT-REC :450-464. case02's seed, so the first transaction is rejected with reason 100 - and the WRITE at :451 is arranged to report a status other than '00'. :450 had already moved 8 into APPL-RESULT, so the ELSE at :454 moves 12, 88 APPL-AOK is false at :457, and :460-463 run: DISPLAY 'ERROR WRITING TO REJECTS FILE', then 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS, then 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM. The status is the permanent-error one a backend refusal reports, whose first character is '9', so 9910 takes its :715-721 arm - the extended one that renders the feedback byte as three digits - and the line reads FILE STATUS IS: NNNN9000. CALL 'CEE3ABD' at :711 does not return, so the six CLOSE paragraphs, both count lines and the closing banner are never reached and RETURN-CODE is 12 rather than the 4 a rejected transaction would otherwise have produced. DALYREJS holds nothing: the record whose write was refused was never stored, and app/jcl/POSTTRAN.jcl:34 declares DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE), whose third positional deletes the generation outright when the step ends abnormally.",
